This paper introduces a modular, expandable Monte Carlo Tree Search framework, specifically designed for the Java Virtual Machine (JVM), that simplifies implementation and execution. By utilizing Java 8's functional interfaces to create lightweight modules, the framework streamlines the search process. We have successfully integrated and evaluated various lightweight search algorithms against their optimized counterparts on the OpenLanTrek game, and found our framework to be a more efficient and generalizable solution, even surpassing the performance of optimized implementations in certain scenarios. We have released the framework's source code under the Apache License 2.0 on GitHub for reference and further exploration. https://github.com/berkeleyearthon/mtree. An accompanying video demonstration is available at https://youtu.be/6lWlQX8s6gA. Our research paper has been submitted for peer review. https://arxiv.org/cts/2021/10.1007/s40032-021-00181-5. \footnote{This work has been submitted for publication. Its current version is available at https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.03535.} 

